diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 62e2b16..bd8a137 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
 
 ## UNRELEASED
 
+- **Add: claude-opus-5-5 model** — Claude Opus 5.5 (released 2026-09-22) is selectable via `/model` and the `opus` shortcut now resolves to it. pi-ai (≤0.87.0) does not list it yet, so `withCatalogFallbacks` synthesizes the entry from `claude-opus-5` until it does, then steps aside. Measured on Max via CC 2.1.280: bare and `[1m]` both serve 1M, so it joins the measured-1M set.
+- **Bump: @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk ^0.3.280** — bundles Claude Code 2.1.280; older CC rejects Opus 5.5 with `400 ... version 2.1.280 or newer is required`.
+
 - **Fix: pi 0.86 transcript contract (issue #106)** — 0.86 folds the system prompt and tool set into `role:"system"` messages instead of `context.systemPrompt`/`context.tools`, so every fresh session took the rebuild path with zero records and `--resume` failed with "No conversation found with session ID". A new `src/transcript.ts` replays the transcript back into the 0.85-shaped `Context` at the stream entry points (and filters system messages in `syncSharedSession`), which also repairs what else 0.86 silently broke: skills/context files not projected to Claude Code (prompt capture resolved nothing), MCP tools never served, compaction and branch summaries throwing on their `[system,user]` context, and cursor arithmetic counting system messages. Sections are re-emitted in pi's canonical render order so the replayed prompt still matches the key prompt capture recorded (a section deleted and re-added — skills while `read`+`bash` are disabled — would otherwise land at the Map tail and fail every later turn). Mid-conversation system messages stay in the transcript space, never enter CC sessions, and the 0.85 path is byte-identical to before.
 - **Fix: pi 0.86 /bug summarization routes through the provider** — 0.86 added `summarizeForBugReport` as a fourth `streamFn` consumer (the streamFn inventory canary caught it at bump time). `runIsolatedSummary` now routes any one-off summarizer call — pi marks them all `cacheRetention: "none"` in `completeSummarization` — instead of requiring the exact compaction `[system,user]` shape, so a future summarizer consumer needs no bridge change. The bug-report prompt reaches CC as its systemPrompt.
 
